<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35968" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">phasma</span></b> , ătis,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάσμα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an apparition</i>,
				<i>spectre</i>, <i>phantom.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The title of a comedy of Menander</i>, <i><span class="en">Ter. Eun.
				prol. 9</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The title</i> or <i>principal part of
				a farce by a mimograph named Catullus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clamosum ut ageres phasma Catulli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					8, 186</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
